---Create a change by repo id
---
---**Accepted credentials:** User token, Plugin installation token.
---
---Creates a trail via the opaque repo id path; behaviour matches the wire-parity create (including the same status policy), and the Location header points back into this addressing scheme.
---
---Use an own-account bearer token (including supported service accounts) or a Core-issued plugin installation bearer token, subject to the permissions and restrictions below. Plugin assertion JWTs and plugin OAuth user-delegation tokens are not accepted here.
---
---Requires live repository push permission (contents:write for plugin installations). Accounts and automation principals may call it; a plugin installation's writes are credited to the installation, so refreshed tokens keep authorship. Trails must be enabled. Send requests to the repository’s primary API region.
---
---`POST /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/changes`
---@param input entire.trails.CreateChangeRequest
---@return entire.trails.TrailCreateResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_change(input) end

