---Delete a merged native Change's branch at its saved head
---
---Answers 204 once the branch is gone, including a branch that was already gone. Open and draft Trails based on the branch are first moved to the base the Trail was merged into, as the caller. A kept branch answers 409 with `code` set to why: moved, protected, default_branch, stacked (a Trail based on it could not be moved) or base; a branch name another Trail has taken answers 409 with `code` branch_claimed, and a merge still finishing 409 with merge_in_progress. A refusal answers 422 or 503 with `code` set to its reason. A branch state that could not be read, a move of a Trail based on it that failed, and any other storage failure carry `code` failed.
---
---`DELETE /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/changes/{number}/branch`
---@param input entire.trails.DeleteChangeBranchRequest
---@return entire.trails.DeleteChangeBranchResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_change_branch(input) end

---Delete a merged native Trail's branch at its saved head
---
---Answers 204 once the branch is gone, including a branch that was already gone. Open and draft Trails based on the branch are first moved to the base the Trail was merged into, as the caller. A kept branch answers 409 with `code` set to why: moved, protected, default_branch, stacked (a Trail based on it could not be moved) or base; a branch name another Trail has taken answers 409 with `code` branch_claimed, and a merge still finishing 409 with merge_in_progress. A refusal answers 422 or 503 with `code` set to its reason. A branch state that could not be read, a move of a Trail based on it that failed, and any other storage failure carry `code` failed.
---
---`DELETE /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/trails/{number}/branch`
---@param input entire.trails.DeleteTrailBranchRequest
---@return entire.trails.DeleteTrailBranchResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_trail_branch(input) end

